  "findings": [
    "NoteBox#getStartingX truncates the component origin and getSegment merges live thickness at both preferred-height endpoints; ComponentRoseNote adds deltaShadow to preferred width and height. Added shadow width and live-segment sampling follow this model. ArrowAndNoteBox combines arrow and note preferred dimensions, not their visible polygons.",
    "All eight primary envelope cases fail. Legacy padding2 with a nested live segment and delay is435px tall in Java versus431px in Rust; shadowed counterparts also fail. Two focused legacy non-self attached-note controls pass, but both Teoz attached-note controls fail, including a10.6553px arrow ordinate displacement.",
    "Self-note placement is separately synthesized from arrow_y-first_height+SELF_MSG_RIGHT_NOTE_Y_PAD at sequence.rs:7397, while other notes subtract padded component contributions. Multi-participant drawing at13218 still builds preferred width without note_shadow_delta and over_several_note_geometry uses painted participant widths. These duplicated component approximations are live dependencies of the claimed envelope and block acceptance.",
    "All14 accounts were present byte-for-byte in earlier chronological commits before their corresponding code. See provenance.json and commit-mapping.json. Main release tiers remain11181/11251 product-library and10497/11251 assisted-library; source-only CLI cohort403/955 with10 invalid references; no regressions observed.",
    "Verdict applies to whole source-to-SVG recovery with the dependencies described above. Positive component-local observations are explicitly bounded and are not acceptance. Every mismatch and negative remains in the standing suite."
  ],
